                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2]Yea containment is an understatement... I was puzzled by that[/h2]\r\n\r\nIn Containment the Zombie Puzzler it's a game that... well, puzzles you. No, I mean you have to solve puzzles that are, well... puzzling. No, that's not right either. Let me start over.\r\n\r\nContainment the Zombie Puzzler isn't really a puzzle game. It's more of a strategy game. The strategy is to contain zombies with matching units fast enough to prevent more zombies from being created.\r\n\r\nThe moment you launch the game you're greeted by a continuous dial tone. No music. Just a dial tone. I guess a zombie left the phone off the hook. Then once you start the campaign you quickly realize why I put the game down 11 years ago. It's very repetitive, and after a while it starts feeling more like work than fun.\r\n\r\nIronic that there are achievements for killing survivors. That's not exactly the definition of surviving now, is it?\r\n\r\nAnyhoo... I lightly recommend this game because there are better games out there and it feels unfinished, but it's not terrible.\r\n\r\n[h2]6/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h3][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h3]",
